<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<class name="AbilitySystemComponent" inherits="Node" api_type="extension" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot/master/doc/class.xsd">
	<brief_description>
		Node that owns a pawn abilities, gameplay tags, effects and attributes.
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		The hub of the ability system. Grants and activates [GameplayAbility] resources, applies [GameplayEffect]s, counts owned gameplay tags and holds an [AttributeSet].
		The attribute set is duplicated at runtime, so the resource on disk is a template and is never mutated by play.
		Owned tags are reference counted: the same tag granted by two sources needs both to release it before it is gone. That is why one ability ending does not strip a tag another ability still grants.
		C# scripts cannot inherit GDExtension classes, so consume this compositionally - place the node, author the resources, call the methods and connect to the signals.
	</description>
